{"availability":"available","full":"johnmn3/cljs-thread","name":"cljs-thread","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Clojure","stars":59,"forks":0,"created":"2022-07-05T00:05:24Z","updated":"2026-03-10T12:11:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://johnmn3.github.io/cljs-thread/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.393Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.393Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.393Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.513Z","stars":59,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:34:38.628Z","stars":59,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T04:04:58.238Z","stars":59,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.393Z","stars":59,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["cljs-thread makes using webworkers take less... work. Eventually, I'd like it to be able to minimize the amount of build tool configuration it takes to spawn workers in Clojurescript too, but that's a longer term goal.","When you spawn a node, it automatically creates connections to all the other nodes, creating a fully connected mesh.","The in macro then abstracts over the message passing infrastructure, with implicit binding conveyance and blocking semantics, allowing you to do work on threads in a manner similar to what you would experience with threads in Clojure and other languages. cljs-thread provides familiar constructs like future, pmap, pcalls and pvalues. For transducing over large sequences in parallel, the =>> thread-last macro is provided."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/johnmn3/cljs-thread/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"98cb26e8ad980672a952ac88e756ca6cf2ddf728ef3747af3b092363cd682bb0","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:28.691Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.489Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"cljs-thread makes using webworkers take less... work. Eventually, I'd like it to be able to minimize the amount of build tool configuration it takes to spawn workers in Clojurescript too, but that's a longer term goal.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/johnmn3/cljs-thread/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"A single synchronous in call will cost you around 4 to 5 milliseconds, depending on if it needs to be proxied.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/johnmn3/cljs-thread/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"cljs-thread's blocking semantics are great for achieving synchronous control flow when you need it, but as shown above, it has a performance cost of having to wait on the service worker to proxy results.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/johnmn3/cljs-thread/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"98cb26e8ad980672a952ac88e756ca6cf2ddf728ef3747af3b092363cd682bb0","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/johnmn3/cljs-thread/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.489Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-03-10T12:11:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/johnmn3/cljs-thread/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.490Z","hash":"98cb26e8ad980672a952ac88e756ca6cf2ddf728ef3747af3b092363cd682bb0","originalBytes":20442,"storedBytes":20442,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:16:43.393Z","subjects":[],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Other","subjects":[],"evidence":[],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":[],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://johnmn3.github.io/cljs-thread/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-14T13:41:18.937Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-14T13:41:18.937Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-14T13:41:18.937Z","target":"https://johnmn3.github.io/cljs-thread/","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-21T13:41